+# Builder Access Point — v0.6
+
+A human browser and an AI/programmatic author must use the same semantic mutation model.
+
+## Human path
+
+```text
+rendered Builder Studio form
+  -> UI_ACTION DESIGN.*.DRAFT
+  -> Wire UI Server validation
+  -> WireUIBuilderApplication
+  -> WireUIDesignOperation
+  -> target WireUIBuilderProject
+```
+
+## AI/programmatic path
+
+```text
+typed proposal/tooling
+  -> WireUIDesignOperation
+  -> target WireUIBuilderProject
+```
+
+Both paths use project compare-and-swap revision semantics.
+
+The current first-party Studio exposes component, element, projection, material, journey, two-variant experiment and composition editors, a direct-manipulation composition canvas, compiled preview controls, plus explicit publication. These are intentionally generic authoring concepts; applications supply their own semantic vocabulary as target-project data.
+
+The Builder action adapter is not an authentication boundary. The owning Wire UI application/server authorises the subject before an action reaches project mutation logic.
+
+
+## Visual manipulation path
+
+```text
+canvas drag
+  -> UI_ACTION DESIGN.COMPOSITION.MOVE
+  -> Server action binding / revision / ownership validation
+  -> WireUIBuilderApplication
+  -> WireUIDesignOperation
+  -> target project composition draft
+```
+
+Selection (`COMPOSITION.SELECT`) and movement (`DESIGN.COMPOSITION.MOVE`) are separate semantic actions on the same canvas instance. Wire UI Server v0.11 adds backwards-compatible multiple bound actions per instance; each action still requires explicit availability at the rendered revision.
+
+## v0.6 direct manipulation
+
+The canvas now exposes four independent typed mutations:
+
+```text
+DESIGN.COMPOSITION.MOVE       reorder placements
+DESIGN.COMPOSITION.RESIZE     span / rowSpan
+DESIGN.COMPOSITION.RELOCATE   semantic region
+DESIGN.COMPOSITION.ALIGN      START / CENTER / END / STRETCH
+```
+
+The screen-flow filmstrip is derived from target journey states/transitions and composition layout signatures. Selecting a flow state is a normal `FLOW.SELECT` Server action; it changes the preview context and scopes the canvas to that state.
+
+Library/canvas/inspector region stacks are browser presentation only. The authoritative Studio instances, target composition drafts, Server ownership checks and project revision ledger remain unchanged.
