+# HTTP front qualification — one variable only
+
+Purpose: prove whether the Wire UI Builder browser access point behaves identically when only the HTTP front changes. This is an A/B qualification tool, not a deployment architecture change.
+
+Freeze all of the following for both runs:
+
+- staged `web/` and `runtime/` bytes;
+- `/wire-ui/bootstrap` semantic JSON;
+- Queue Fabric WebSocket gateway and its port;
+- private Queue Fabric bridge/application host;
+- Wire UI Server state, definitions and queues;
+- browser/runtime package versions.
+
+Only the HTTP front process may change.
+
+## Capture the existing front
+
+```
+tools/capture_http_front_contract.sh http://127.0.0.1:8765 /tmp/front-node /tmp/wire-ui-builder-live/site
+```
+
+Record SOURCE and DESIGN behaviour without changing source.
+
+## Substitute only the HTTP front
+
+Stop only the process owning port 8765. Keep the WebSocket gateway and private ooRexx host alive. Start ooRexx HTTPS/HTTP serving the identical staged tree and an equivalent `/wire-ui/bootstrap` response.
+
+Capture it:
+
+```
+tools/capture_http_front_contract.sh http://127.0.0.1:8765 /tmp/front-oorexx /tmp/wire-ui-builder-live/site
+```
+
+Compare:
+
+```
+tools/compare_http_front_contract.sh /tmp/front-node /tmp/front-oorexx
+```
+
+Acceptance requires matching HTTP payload hashes, normalized bootstrap JSON and (when supplied) staged site-tree hashes. SOURCE/DESIGN behaviour is then compared separately.
+
+Do not repair DESIGN, rewrite bootstrap JavaScript, change Queue Fabric, change the WebSocket gateway, or introduce an HTTP business API during this experiment.
