+# notNotes Web Wire reference
+
+## Sources checked
+
+This Builder increment was compared against:
+
+- `notnotes_windows_client_v0.1-dev1.zip`
+  - SHA-256 `1882ac0e3ce2c3d3ac144b15478dc64c31095d8a78c55c34d8348fc6cc54bf35`
+  - Windows design contract: left rail, virtualised register, right context panel, bottom intention composer/activity.
+  - Its own documentation correctly says dev1 is still a smoke shell and not a complete NotNotes Windows client.
+- `notnotes_mini_approval_app_v0.1-dev13.zip`
+  - SHA-256 `c8efcfd1090555aabeecae6cf693ea518695f78bf9d601170a485c2dc5dc5ace`
+  - authoritative current application capabilities used to fill control gaps left by the Windows smoke shell.
+
+The Web reference therefore seeks **semantic capability parity with the Windows target plus current NotNotes**, not pixel parity with the incomplete Win32 dev1 executable.
+
+## Desktop web layout
+
+```text
+┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│ notNotes                         connection/revision                 refresh  │
+├──────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────┤
+│ Home         │ Search / filter / sort / commands    │ Context/detail        │
+│ Documents    ├───────────────────────────────────────┤ fields                │
+│ TPS Reports  │                                       │ relationships         │
+│ Approvals    │ virtualised document/report register │ lifecycle             │
+│ Help Desk    │                                       │ print/export          │
+│              ├───────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────┤
+│              │ activity / result freshness                                   │
+├──────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
+│ Ask notNotes / clarification / dynamic intention discovery / End Session     │
+└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+Narrow layouts may collapse the left rail and context panel while retaining the same semantic states/actions.
+
+## notNotes control coverage
+
+### Register and discovery
+
+- Documents / views / TPS reports / approvals navigation.
+- Query/search.
+- Filter and explicit saved-view selection.
+- Sort.
+- Bounded virtual document register.
+- Stable selection/open identity.
+- Fresh-window/revision refresh.
+
+### Document detail and editing
+
+- Read/detail surface.
+- Typed field editing.
+- explicit Save / application flush.
+- Print / PDF affordance.
+- Relationship picker for one and many `DOCUMENT_REFERENCE` values.
+- Link / unlink selected references.
+- Embedded subview projection and calculated totals.
+
+### Lifecycle
+
+- Submit.
+- Approve.
+- Reject.
+- Current lifecycle/status badge.
+
+These are ordinary NotNotes semantic actions. The browser does not decide whether a transition is legal.
+
+### Format and document construction
+
+- Design new format.
+- Improve/alter an existing format additively.
+- Complete/create a document from a format.
+- Add fields with appropriate control projections.
+- Add subviews.
+- Add row/column calculations.
+
+Existing field-contract protection remains a NotNotes rule rather than a browser rule.
+
+### Saved reports and output
+
+- List saved report definitions.
+- Run saved report.
+- Design report.
+- Print/PDF.
+- Export XLSX / ODS / CSV / TSV through the existing Spreadsheet authority.
+
+### Help Desk / intentions
+
+The bottom composer maps to the Initech/NotNotes intention-facing session surface:
+
+- fresh `DiscoverIntentions` before each turn;
+- `SubmitText`;
+- bounded clarification choices;
+- current activity/result display;
+- End Session, allowing the helpdesk authority to persist the TPS process evidence/review.
+
+The Web release may carry a stable `WireUIIntentionRequirement`, but it must never seal a provider result, confidence score, slot value, feasibility result or stale `READY` decision.
+
+## Semantic action surface in the reference fixture
+
+```text
