+# Builder ↔ Wire UI Runtime Meeting Point — v0.6
+
+The Builder is an authoring application above the Wire UI runtime; consumer applications are not part of this contract.
+
+## Compiled target package
+
+v0.4 preserves the established compiled interaction package contract. Exact definitions retain:
+
+```text
+definitionId
+exact definitionVersion
+definitionKey = definitionId@version
+contentAddress
+semanticElementRef
+projectionRef
+componentRef
+profile
+material/style roles
+```
+
+No runtime path needs `WireUIBuilderProject` merely to serve an already published target release.
+
+## Builder Studio application
+
+The Builder itself is also served as Wire UI. `WireUIBuilderRuntimeFactory` takes:
+
+- a separate target `WireUIBuilderProject`;
+- optional source catalogue;
+- application/session/access-point identity;
+- preferably the precompiled `wire_ui_builder_studio_v0.6.json`.
+
+It creates a `WireUIBuilderApplication`, binds the Studio compiled release through Server v0.11 and installs target-project/source state into the Studio view.
+
+Browser form and composition actions return as normal `UI_ACTION` messages and are revalidated by the server before the Builder application converts them to typed draft operations.
+
+## Server v0.11
+
+Server v0.11 provides exact release binding, renderer-profile manifests, material delivery, dynamic journey advancement and authorised `CREATE_INSTANCE` patches. Builder v0.4 uses those existing semantics rather than defining a private Builder transport.
+
+## Browser path
+
+The web shell expects the normal Queue Fabric gateway bootstrap contract and Alchemy Wire UI JS. It contains no hard-coded `DESIGN.*.DRAFT` business implementation: those actions arrive from the Studio's compiled definitions.
+
+```text
+browser shell
+  -> Queue Fabric gateway transport
+  -> Wire UI Server v0.11
+  -> WireUIBuilderApplication
+  -> target WireUIBuilderProject
+```
+
+## Protocol version
+
+`WIRE-UI/0.1` remains sufficient. Builder v0.4 changes the authoring model, not the fundamental Wire UI transport protocol.
+
+
+## Composition metadata
+
+The compiled package may contain additive `compositions`, and definition metadata may contain `compositionHints`. These are renderer/preview hints bound to exact authoring artifacts; they do not change action authority, state authority or the `WIRE-UI/0.1` message protocol.
