+# Wire UI modern web control catalogue
+
+The web catalogue is a renderer-neutral set of visual primitives for modern application workspaces. It is deliberately **not** a DOM component library and does not make browser controls authoritative.
+
+A Builder release may project the same semantic element through these primitives on Web while Windows, Swing, GTK, Android or direct Linux use different native controls. Cross-renderer equivalence is defined by semantic element identity, action identity, state, revisions and evidence—not by pixels or widget classes.
+
+## Catalogue
+
+### Application / navigation
+
+- `APP_SHELL` — responsive application shell and landmarks.
+- `NAV_RAIL` — primary navigation rail/drawer.
+- `COMMAND_BAR` — contextual commands and overflow actions.
+- `TAB_SET` — keyboard-operable semantic tabs.
+- `DIALOG` — modal/sheet projection with focus containment.
+
+### Discovery / collection controls
+
+- `SEARCH_BOX` — semantic search input.
+- `FILTER_BAR` — multi-filter/chip surface.
+- `SORT_CONTROL` — explicit sort field/direction selection.
+- `VIRTUAL_TABLE` — bounded/windowed row source; stable row identity; keyboard navigation; optional multi-selection.
+- `SUBVIEW_TABLE` — relationship-backed embedded collection with calculated rows/totals.
+- `REPORT_VIEW` — saved report projection with bounded rows, summary, export and print affordances.
+
+`VIRTUAL_TABLE` and `REPORT_VIEW` must never imply that the renderer owns the full backing collection. A visible window is a projection of an authoritative source.
+
+### Detail / editing
+
+- `DETAIL_PANEL`
+- `FORM` v2
+- `TEXT_FIELD`
+- `TEXT_AREA`
+- `NUMBER_FIELD`
+- `DATE_FIELD`
+- `SELECT_FIELD`
+- `MULTI_SELECT`
+- `CHECKBOX`
+- `RADIO_GROUP`
+- `RELATION_PICKER`
+
+`RELATION_PICKER` works with stable semantic identities. It is suitable for one-to-one and one-to-many document/object references and must not turn display row numbers into relationship identity.
+
+### Actions / state / feedback
+
+- `ACTION_BUTTON`
+- `ACTION_GROUP`
+- `STATUS_BADGE`
+- `ACTIVITY_FEED`
+- `PROGRESS_STATUS`
+- `TOAST`
+
+Buttons emit semantic actions. A disabled/hidden renderer control is presentation of server/application availability; it is not permission authority.
+
+### Intention interaction
+
+- `INTENTION_COMPOSER` — multiline natural-language turn entry, dynamic discovery and clarification-aware presentation.
+- `CLARIFICATION_CHOICES` — bounded choices and/or free-text clarification.
+
+The control catalogue does not contain an LLM or an Intention Service implementation. Runtime-discovered intentions are evidence/capability state. The Builder may seal stable intention requirements only; discovery and `READY` are refreshed at runtime.
+
+## Responsive presentation
+
+The catalogue supports different layouts without changing application semantics. A desktop browser may show rail + register + context panel + composer simultaneously. A narrow browser may project the same semantics as navigation → register → detail with a bottom composer. Renderer-specific layout is expected; semantic action and identity drift is not.
+
+## Accessibility baseline
+
+Web renderers should implement native HTML semantics first, keyboard navigation, labelled controls, focus visibility, accessible status/live regions, reduced-motion preference, and modality/focus containment where required. Visual styling must not be the only representation of state.
+
+## Resource-import primitives
+
+The catalogue also exposes renderer-neutral projections required by the Windows/resource executable-tree bridge: `LABEL`, `GROUP_BOX`, `LIST_BOX`, `RADIO_OPTION`, `IMAGE`, `SCROLL_BAR`, `MENU`, `MENU_ITEM`, and `RESOURCE_CONTROL`.
+
+`RESOURCE_CONTROL` is intentionally a fail-closed fallback for a resource object whose native control class has not yet acquired an exact portable projection. It preserves semantic/resource identity and trigger bindings without pretending the browser understands an unknown Win32 control.
